# tally 2.2 (CHANGES.md 2.2-10, plan §3, choice C-2 (a)). E §3.2: a def's cell is kept under its context trimmed to
# what the def can depend on, and a def keyed by a movement depends on the movement. The dependency graph had no edge
# for a def's own key over an event kind, where an aggregate's binding over the same kind records the kind and its
# moves, so in_pln's cone held no movement and no axis: h and h2 printed one line [work = *], 400.00 PLN, the cell
# computed once under the first option. With the edge, the helper def splits as the inline sum i does: 100.00 EUR at
# 4 under yes, 300.00 EUR under no. hp, a pin of amt[yes] under work = yes, reaches the def: 2 000.00 PLN.
=== m.tally
model fx1
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-10
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
unit EUR: currency minor 0.01
axis work
  yes "in work"
  no "not in work"
place wallet: accounts EUR lives 2025-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input fx: num PLN/EUR
input d1: date
input amt[w in work]: money EUR
input mo: month

def pay: money EUR at reader
  rule base = amt[work]

move in1: transfers
  on d1
  at d1
  leg cash from world to wallet amount pay

def in_pln[t in transfers]: money PLN = round(t.cash.amount * fx, minor(PLN), half-up) at t.day

def by_inline: money PLN at reader
  rule base = sum(round(t.cash.amount * fx, minor(PLN), half-up) for t in transfers over mo where t.cash.to == wallet)
def by_helper: money PLN at reader
  rule base = sum(in_pln[t] for t in transfers over mo where t.cash.to == wallet)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  d1 = 2026-03-05 "s"
  amt[yes] = 100.00 EUR "s"
  amt[no] = 300.00 EUR "s"
  mo = 2026-03 "s"
  fx = 4.0 "s"
  opening[wallet] = 0.00 EUR at 2026-01-01 start "s"

ask i: by_inline law 2026-06-01
ask h: by_helper law 2026-06-01
ask h2: in_pln[t] for t in transfers over 2026-03 law 2026-06-01
ask hp: by_helper, by_helper as if {amt[yes] = 500.00 EUR}, by_inline as if {amt[yes] = 500.00 EUR} with work = yes law 2026-06-01
=== expect i h h2 hp
i [work = yes]: 400.00 PLN
  reading: work = yes
  unfulfilled: in1
  law date 2026-06-01, cut 2026-06-10
i [work = no]: 1 200.00 PLN
  reading: work = no
  unfulfilled: in1
  law date 2026-06-01, cut 2026-06-10
h [work = yes]: 400.00 PLN
  reading: work = yes
  unfulfilled: in1
  law date 2026-06-01, cut 2026-06-10
h [work = no]: 1 200.00 PLN
  reading: work = no
  unfulfilled: in1
  law date 2026-06-01, cut 2026-06-10
h2 (t = in1) [work = yes]: 400.00 PLN
  reading: work = yes
  unfulfilled: in1
  law date 2026-06-01, cut 2026-06-10
h2 (t = in1) [work = no]: 1 200.00 PLN
  reading: work = no
  unfulfilled: in1
  law date 2026-06-01, cut 2026-06-10
hp: (400.00 PLN, 2 000.00 PLN, 2 000.00 PLN)
  pinned: amt[yes] = 500.00 EUR
  pinned: work = yes
  unfulfilled: in1
  law date 2026-06-01, cut 2026-06-10
